model_response:
{"response": "It's completely understandable to have feelings for someone you've had a crush on for years. Reaching out after some time can be nerve-wracking but also an opportunity to reconnect and see how both of your lives have changed since high school. If you're feeling anxious about it, taking a moment to reflect on why this person is important to you might help clarify your intentions.

Before reaching out, consider sending him a friendly message asking how he's been doing in general terms. This can be less pressure than directly discussing feelings and allows for an easy conversation if he responds positively. If there's no response after a few days, it’s okay not to push the issue further. Remember, reconnecting is about mutual interest and respect.

If you're feeling overwhelmed by these emotions or any related anxiety, talking to someone who can provide support might be helpful. Consider reaching out to friends, family members, or even a counselor for additional guidance."}

"citations": ["WHO Depression Fact Sheet — Symptoms and patterns", "NIMH Depression — Find help and support", "NIMH Anxiety Disorders — Find help and support"]}

